          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20400 o2iblnd: fix descriptor leak on FastReg map error",
        "message": "LU-20400 o2iblnd: fix descriptor leak on FastReg map error\n\nkiblnd_fmr_pool_map() removes a fast registration descriptor from\nfpo->fast_reg.fpo_pool_list and bumps fpo->fpo_map_count before\ncalling ib_map_mr_sg(). When ib_map_mr_sg() short-maps the\nscatterlist (n != rd->rd_nfrags), the function returns the error\nwithout returning the descriptor to the pool and without dropping\nthe map count. It also leaves fmr->fmr_frd and fmr->fmr_pool NULL,\nso the caller's kiblnd_fmr_pool_unmap() is a no-op and cannot\nrecover them.\n\nEach short-map therefore leaks one descriptor and one pool\nreference. Because fpo_map_count never returns to zero,\nkiblnd_fmr_pool_is_idle() never reports the pool idle, so it is\nnever reaped. Under a workload that produces gapped transfers\n(which fail ib_map_mr_sg() repeatedly) the FMR pool grows without\nbound.\n\nOn the error path, reacquire fps_lock, return the descriptor to\nfpo_pool_list, mark it not posted, and decrement fpo_map_count, the\nsame cleanup kiblnd_fmr_pool_unmap() performs. fmr_frd and fmr_pool\nare intentionally left NULL.\n\nAdd a fault-injection point, CFS_FAIL_O2IBLND_FMR_MAP_SHORT\n(0xf101), that forces a short-map result so the cleanup path can be\nexercised deterministically without a real gapped layout. With the\nleak present, fpo_map_count never returns to zero and\nkiblnd_destroy_fmr_pool()'s LASSERT(fpo_map_count == 0) fires on\nmodule unload; with the fix, unload is clean.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I9580a6ebc9fd7056c0450cca912f613491ee908d\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
